.TH DEDIT 1.SH NAMEdedit \- disk sector editor.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdedit\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBdedit\fRreads, changes and writes the raw sectors of an RBF disk.  It asks for adevice pathlist, shows a sector as hex and characters with its address,and takes single-letter commands from a menu along the bottom:\fBD\fRchanges drive,\fBE\fRedits the bytes on screen,\fBF\fRshows a file descriptor,\fBL\fRgoes to a logical sector number you enter,\fBM\fRshows the allocation map sector and\fBS\fRdecodes the disk's identification sector; the up and down arrows stepto the previous and next sector..PPIt sets the terminal\fBnopause noecho\fRwith\fBtmode\fRwhile it runs, and back to\fBpause echo\fRwhen it finishes..SH NOTES\fBdedit\fRis BASIC09 I-code, not 68000 code: nine procedures packed in one file.Run it with Microware's\fBrunb\fRloaded, by its bare name.  It writes to the disk you give it, so try iton a copy first..SH SEE ALSOdump, fstat, rsdsk